-- Template for infra/seed/resume.sql, which is gitignored because it holds
-- real resume text (AGENTS.md rule 9's corollary: the resume never enters
-- this public repository). Copy this file to resume.sql and replace the
-- placeholder text below with your own resume content, then run
-- `make seed-resume`.
--
-- See resume.sql's own header (once you've created it) for the full
-- explanation of the $resume$ ... $resume$ dollar-quoting and the
-- ON CONFLICT UPDATE behavior.

INSERT INTO resume (user_id, raw_text)
SELECT
    id,
    $resume$Jane Doe

Summary
Replace this entire block with your own resume's text content. Keep it
plain text — no PDF formatting artifacts. resume_match's semantic term
embeds this text; the keyword term checks skill-name presence directly
against it, so include the substance (experience, projects, skills) that
you want matched against job postings.

Omit your phone number and any other field with zero matching value —
it adds nothing to resume_match and is the most sensitive single field on
most resumes.
$resume$
FROM app_user
WHERE email = :'user_email'
ON CONFLICT (user_id) DO UPDATE SET
    raw_text = excluded.raw_text,
    embedding = NULL,
    embedding_version = NULL,
    updated_at = now();
